    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d639">

                <pb facs="0904" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1906p1/pg798"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Second Assistant Secretary of
                            State to Consul Proffit.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-03-16"><hi rendition="#italic">March 16,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 47.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have to acknowledge the receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 68, of January 28 last, in regard to the refusal of the British
                    authorities to pay the bonds, issued by the Boer government, which are now held
                    by Dr. William H. McGreevy.</p>
                <p>You will please forward to the department a copy of the decision of the
                    commission by which payment was denied.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
